# API Service Selection

- When adding API/data calls, first check `apps/web/src/lib/services` for an existing service that already owns that domain.
- Reuse the correct service when possible instead of adding ad-hoc fetch logic inside pages/components.
- If no service fits, create a new focused service file with a clear domain name (for example `orders.service.ts`).
- Keep service responsibilities narrow: one domain per service, explicit exported functions, predictable inputs/outputs.
- UI components should call service functions (directly or through hooks), not build low-level request logic inline.
- Keep transport/error normalization in services where possible.
- If a new endpoint touches an existing domain, extend the existing service instead of creating duplicates.
